    "origin_id": "https://www.autoevolution.com/news/2027-toyota-sienna-released-with-tons-of-changes-throws-more-power-to-the-road-278746.html",
    "canonical_url": "https://www.autoevolution.com/news/2027-toyota-sienna-released-with-tons-of-changes-throws-more-power-to-the-road-278746.html",
    "origin_publisher": "autoevolution",
    "published_at": "2026-11-20T15:05:28+00:00",
    "published_at_raw": "2026-11-20T15:05:28+0000",
    "publication_precision": "TIMESTAMP",
    "acquired_at": "2026-11-20T18:15:03.302594+00:00",
    "available_at": "2026-11-20T18:15:03.302594+00:00",
    "body": "EICMA 2026 • Here Are Some of the Serious and Obscure Brands That EICMA 2026 Had To Offer – Worth Knowing About\n2027 Toyota Sienna Released with Tons of Changes, Throws More Power to the Road\n29 photos\nPhoto: Toyota\nMinivans of America, beware! The 2027 Toyota Sienna is coming for you, and this time it brings along much more than just a visual makeover and some extra creature comforts – the changes the Japanese carmaker has planned include more power from the hybrid system, more safety features, and extra technology.\nScheduled to hit Toyota dealers across the U.S. early next year, the biggest change the 2027 Sienna brings along is the new 6th-generation hybrid system. Everything about it is different from before, including the internal combustion engine, the electric motors, and the battery pack.\nBuilt from the ground up with larger vehicles that need higher-capacity hybrid hardware in mind, the tech is centered around a 2.5-liter engine, a 124-kW electric drive motor (and also another 40-kW motor for the rear axle in all-wheel drive versions), and a 1.15 kWh lithium-ion battery.\nThe 6th gen delivers a combined 251 horsepower, which is up six horsepower from before. A minuscule increase, you could argue, but do keep in mind that we're talking about a people mover, not a race car. Torque levels, on the other hand, remain the same as before, 176 lb.-ft.\nThe new power levels allow the Sienna in front-wheel-drive configuration to accelerate from standstill to 60 mph in 7.5 seconds, something that will definitely make the kids in the back feel like they're in a fighter jet taking off from the deck of an aircraft carrier.\nPhoto: Toyota The engine has a fuel consumption rating, as measured by Toyota, of 39 mpg (six liters/100 km) in city driving, some three mpg better than before. The highway and combined ratings stand at 35 and 37 mpg, respectively.\nToyota revealed it has also tampered with the minivan's handling by fitting new electronic power steering components, including a new steering column and steering wheel. The steering gearbox, motor control unit (MCU), and torque sensor are also new, and they should aid the van to minimize steering effort at low speeds and increase on-center definition at highway speeds.\nThe Japanese also upgraded the electrical platform of the 2027 Sienna , and that allowed the deployment of the Toyota Safety Sense 4.0 suite, which makes the model the fourth to get it, following the 2026 RAV4 and 2027 Tundra and Sequoia. This solution packs upgraded sensors and hardware, and also throws in a dash cam as standard.\nAnother mechanical upgrade the new Sienna brings along is the electronically controlled brake system that debuted on the 2026 RAV4. Just like in that application, it is meant to maximize brake feel while also minimizing body roll.\nPhoto: Toyota Finally, the already very quiet cabin of the minivan has been made even more so by the addition of a new, higher-density dash silencer. Supposedly, this hardware will cut the level of noise that enters the cabin by a tiny 1.6 decibels.\nFor the needs of the occupants, the new Sienna is now equipped with a 12.3-inch touchscreen to handle infotainment needs, running Toyota's audio multimedia system. As a reminder, the LE grade of the previous version came with an eight-inch screen.\nThis tech is backed by a 12.3-inch digital gauge cluster that replaces the previous seven-inch screen on the LE and XLE models. An even bigger screen, sized at 12.9 inches, can be had when going for the optional rear seat entertainment center on the Woodland, XSE, and Platinum models.\nSpeaking of trim levels, the 2027 Sienna offering is a tad simpler than it used to be, as it is offered in five trim levels, namely LE, XLE, Woodland, XSE, and Platinum. As you can see, the current Limited is no longer around, as it was made redundant by the upgrades made to the XSE grade. Among them, ventilated seats for driver and right-side passenger, a heads-up display, and a panoramic view monitor, among others.\nPhoto: Toyota Some of the other trim levels come with their own novelties as well. The LE, for instance, is now equipped with a rear lift gate kick sensor that's offered as standard when the towing hitch is not equipped, while the rest of them all get an eight-way power-adjustable front passenger seat. A panoramic view monitor is now standard on the Woodland .\nThe new Sienna will be available in up to three rows of seats, and in an eight-seat configuration with a stowable middle seat. There are also second-row captain’s chairs on the table for seven-seat models.\nThe 2027 Sienna will continue to be assembled at the Toyota facility in Princeton, Indiana, on the Toyota Next Generation-K (TNG-K) platform. As said, the new version will hit the roads early next year, but Toyota keeps its lips tight when it comes to pricing.\nAs a reminder, the present-day Sienna starts at $41,320. It's likely the same color choices available now will apply to the 2027 minivan as well, with the exception of the Cypress exterior paint, which has been discontinued, and with the addition of Storm Cloud.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\ntoyota sienna Toyota minivan\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Daniel Patrascu\nDaniel loves writing (or so he claims), and he uses this skill to offer readers a \"behind the scenes\" look at the automotive industry. He also enjoys talking about space exploration and robots, because in his view the only way forward for humanity is away from this planet, in metal bodies. Full profile\nUP NEXT Subaru's New TY85 Manual-Equipped WRX STI Sport R Clocks Over 1,000 Orders in Less Than Two Days",
